module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExtendScalarsImageProduct
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.ToposThickening.ModulesOnThickening.IdealProduct
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickeningsIdealMap

/-!
# The ideal product of a strict morphism of thickenings

Let

```
  (Sh(C), O)  --i-->  (Sh(D), O')
      |                   |
      f                   f'
      v                   v
  (Sh(B), O_B) --t--> (Sh(B'), O_{B'})
```

be a morphism of thickenings of ringed topoi (Stacks 08M7), with defining ideals
`I = Ker(i^♯) ⊂ O'` and `J = Ker(t^♯) ⊂ O_{B'}`, and let `F'` be a sheaf of `O'`-modules.

This file proves the identity

`(f^{-1}J)F' = I F'`

for a **strict** morphism of thickenings (Stacks 08M9). It is the step of the proof of Stacks
08MQ which says that `F = i^*F'` is the quotient `F'/(f^{-1}J)F'`: the right-hand side is the
ideal product of Stacks 08MP, whose quotient is `i_*i^*F'`
(`Deformation.ToposThickening.idealProductShortComplex_shortExact`), and so the identity is
what turns that sequence into the sequence the source uses.

## The submodule `(f^{-1}J)F'`

The source writes `(f^{-1}J)F'` for the `O'`-submodule of `F'` generated by the local products
of the sections of `J`, read in `O'` through `(f')^♯`, with the sections of `F'`. Both readings
of that submodule are available here and they are proved equal:

* `pullbackIdealProduct` is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.imageProductSubmodule` of the map
  `(f')^*J ⟶ O'` of
  `Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.pullbackIdealToStructure`. This is the
  form in which strictness is stated, Stacks 08M9 asking that the induced map of ideals
  `(f')^*J ⟶ I` be an epimorphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsProductSubmodule inverseImageIdealSections` is the submodule
  generated by the products `(f')^♯(j) • x` with `j` a section of `f^{-1}J` itself, read in `O'`
  through the canonical composite `f^{-1}J ⟶ (f')^*J ⟶ O'` — which is the map
  `f^{-1}J ⟶ I` that Situation 08M7 starts from.

`pullbackIdealProduct_eq_sectionsProductSubmodule` identifies them. That is the statement that
`(f')^*J = O' ⊗_{f^{-1}O_{B'}} f^{-1}J` is generated, as a sheaf of `O'`-modules, by the image
of `f^{-1}J`; it is proved without any pure-tensor decomposition, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.imageProductSubmodule_eq_unitImageSections`.

## Main definitions

* `Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.pullbackIdealProduct`: the submodule
  `(f^{-1}J)F'` of `F'`, generated by the sections of `(f')^*J`.
* `Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.inverseImageIdeal` and
  `.inverseImageIdealUnit`: `f^{-1}J` and the canonical map `f^{-1}J ⟶ (f')^*J`.
* `Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.inverseImageIdealSections`: the sections
  of `f^{-1}J` read in `O'`.

## Main results

In the namespace `Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings`:

* `pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProduct`: **`(f^{-1}J)F' = I F'` for a strict morphism of
  thickenings**, with `I F'` the ideal product of the defining ideal datum of Stacks 08M7.
* `pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProductSubmodule`: the same identity with `I F'` the ideal
  product of Stacks 08MP, i.e. `Deformation.ToposThickening.idealProductSubmodule` of the
  square-zero ideal datum of Stacks 08MB.
* `pullbackIdealProduct_eq_sectionsProductSubmodule`: the two readings of `(f^{-1}J)F'` agree.
* `sectionsProductSubmodule_inverseImageIdealSections_eq_idealProductSubmodule`: the identity
  with both sides written as submodules generated by explicit families of products of sections.

In the namespace `Deformation.ToposThickening`:

* `IdealOfThickening.imageProductSubmodule_incl_eq`: the ideal product does not depend on the
  presentation of the defining ideal — any two presentations have the same sections in `O'`,
  namely the sections killed by `i^♯`.

## Implementation notes

Strictness enters exactly once, and this is the only place where it can: the inclusion
`I F' ⊆ (f^{-1}J)F'` is the assertion that the sections of `I` are *locally* images of sections
of `(f')^*J`, which is local surjectivity of `(f')^*J ⟶ I`, which is strictness. The reverse
inclusion `(f^{-1}J)F' ⊆ I F'` is unconditional, being the factorisation of `(f')^*J ⟶ O'`
through `I` that Stacks 08M7 provides. Both are instances of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.imageProductSubmodule_comp_of_epi`, which is where the locality argument
lives; nothing about the construction of `(f')^*` is used there either.

The identification with the ideal product of Stacks 08MP goes through the sectionwise range of
the inclusion of the ideal rather than through an isomorphism of the two ideal data: both
ranges are the kernel of `i^♯` at each object, and the ideal product depends on the inclusion
only through its range.

The statements about a general defining ideal datum keep the four topoi at independent section
universes. The ones that mention `Deformation.ToposThickening.idealProductSubmodule` put the
two upper topoi at one section universe, which is what that definition is stated at.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08MQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08MQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08M7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08M7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08M9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08M9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08MP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08MP)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry (RingedTopos RingedToposHom)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules (imageProductSubmodule imageProductSubmodule_congr_range
  imageProductSubmodule_comp_of_epi)
open Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules (inverseImageModules fSharpCommRing
  extendRestrictScalarsAdjunction commRingSheafMap)
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward (inverseImageRingSheaf)

universe v u w v' u' w' v'' u'' w'' v''' u''' w'''

namespace Deformation.ToposThickening

section Ideal

variable {X : RingedTopos.{v, u, w}} {Y : RingedTopos.{v', u', w'}}
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})] [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w'})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w'} RingCat.{w'})]
  {i : RingedToposHom X Y}

/-- **The sections of a defining ideal, read in the structure sheaf, are the sections killed by
the structure map.** This is the content of the two characterising fields of
`Deformation.ToposThickening.IdealOfThickening`, assembled into an equality of subsets. -/
theorem IdealOfThickening.range_incl (hI : IdealOfThickening i) (U : Y.Cᵒᵖ) :
    Set.range (fun b : hI.I.val.obj U =>
        (show (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O).obj.obj U from hI.incl.val.app U b)) =
      {a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O).obj.obj U | i.fSharp.hom.app U a = 0} := by
  ext a
  refine ⟨?_, fun ha => hI.exists_section U a ha⟩
  rintro ⟨b, rfl⟩
  exact hI.fSharp_incl_apply U b

/-- **The ideal product does not depend on the presentation of the defining ideal.** Two
presentations of `I = Ker(i^♯)` have the same sections in `O'`, so they multiply the same
submodule out of a sheaf of `O'`-modules. -/
theorem IdealOfThickening.imageProductSubmodule_incl_eq (hI hI' : IdealOfThickening i)
    (F' : SheafOfModules.{w'} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) :
    imageProductSubmodule hI.incl F' = imageProductSubmodule hI'.incl F' :=
  imageProductSubmodule_congr_range F' fun U =>
    (hI.range_incl U).trans (hI'.range_incl U).symm

end Ideal

namespace MorphismOfThickenings

section Strict

variable {X : RingedTopos.{v, u, w}} {X' : RingedTopos.{v', u', w'}}
  {S : RingedTopos.{v'', u'', w''}} {S' : RingedTopos.{v''', u''', w'''}}
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})] [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w'})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w''})] [S'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w'''})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w'} RingCat.{w'})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w''} RingCat.{w''})]
  [S'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w'''} RingCat.{w'''})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w'})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w''})]
  [S'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w'''})]
  [HasWeakSheafify X'.J AddCommGrpCat.{w'}]
  [X'.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w'}]
  (D : MorphismOfThickenings X X' S S')

/-- **The submodule `(f^{-1}J)F'` of `F'`.** The smallest sheaf submodule of `F'` containing
every local product of a section of `(f')^*J`, read in `O'` through
`Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.pullbackIdealToStructure`, with a section of
`F'`. This is the submodule the source writes `(f^{-1}J)F'`: it is generated by the products of
the sections of `f^{-1}J` alone, which is `pullbackIdealProduct_eq_sectionsProductSubmodule`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackIdealProduct
    (F' : SheafOfModules.{w'} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O)) : F'.Submodule :=
  imageProductSubmodule D.pullbackIdealToStructure F'

/-! #### `(f^{-1}J)F'` through the sections of `f^{-1}J` -/

/-- `f^{-1}J`: the inverse image of the lower defining ideal, a sheaf of `f^{-1}O_{B'}`-modules
on the upper topos. -/
noncomputable def inverseImageIdeal : SheafOfModules.{w'}
    (inverseImageRingSheaf D.f'.toModulesHom.toToposHom
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S'.O)) :=
  (inverseImageModules D.f'.toModulesHom.toToposHom
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S'.O)).obj D.idealJ.I

/-- The structure map of `f'` in its inverse-image form `f^{-1}O_{B'} ⟶ O'`, as a morphism of
sheaves of rings. This is the map along which `(f')^*` extends scalars. -/
noncomputable def inverseImageStructureRingMap :
    inverseImageRingSheaf D.f'.toModulesHom.toToposHom
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S'.O) ⟶
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O :=
  commRingSheafMap X'.J (fSharpCommRing D.f'.toModulesHom)
    (inverseImageRingSheaf D.f'.toModulesHom.toToposHom
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S'.O)).property
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O).property

/-- The extension-of-scalars half of the pullback `(f')^* = O' ⊗_{f^{-1}O_{B'}} f^{-1}(-)`, with
its adjunction: `(f')^*` is the inverse image followed by this. -/
noncomputable def extendScalarsAdj :
    Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.extendScalarsFSharp D.f'.toModulesHom ⊣
      SheafOfModules.restrictScalars D.inverseImageStructureRingMap :=
  extendRestrictScalarsAdjunction X'.J (fSharpCommRing D.f'.toModulesHom)
    (inverseImageRingSheaf D.f'.toModulesHom.toToposHom
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S'.O)).property
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O).property

/-- **The canonical map `f^{-1}J ⟶ (f')^*J`**, the unit of the extension of scalars. Composed
with `pullbackIdealToStructure` it is the map `f^{-1}J ⟶ I ⊂ O'` that Situation 08M7 starts
from. -/
noncomputable def inverseImageIdealUnit :
    D.inverseImageIdeal ⟶ (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars D.inverseImageStructureRingMap).obj
      (D.f'.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj D.idealJ.I) :=
  D.extendScalarsAdj.unit.app D.inverseImageIdeal

/-- **The sections of `f^{-1}J`, read in `O'`.** The sectionwise image of the canonical composite

`f^{-1}J ⟶ (f')^*J ⟶ O'`,

the first map being the unit of the extension of scalars and the second
`Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.pullbackIdealToStructure`. This composite is
the map `f^{-1}J ⟶ I ⊂ O'` of Situation 08M7, assembled from the two canonical maps rather than
constructed again from `(f')^♯`; the sections in this family are what the source writes
`(f')^♯(j)`. -/
noncomputable def inverseImageIdealSections (U : X'.Cᵒᵖ) :
    Set ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O).obj.obj U) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.unitImageSections D.inverseImageIdealUnit D.pullbackIdealToStructure U

variable [HasSheafify X'.J AddCommGrpCat.{w'}]

omit [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w''})] in
/-- **The submodule `(f^{-1}J)F'` is generated by the products of the sections of `f^{-1}J`
with the sections of `F'`.** The sections of `(f')^*J` give nothing more: `(f')^*J` is the
extension of scalars of `f^{-1}J`, so a map out of it that kills the image of `f^{-1}J` is zero,
and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.imageProductSubmodule_eq_unitImageSections` turns that into the
equality of the two generated submodules. No pure-tensor decomposition of `(f')^*J` is
used. -/
theorem pullbackIdealProduct_eq_sectionsProductSubmodule
    (F' : SheafOfModules.{w'} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O)) :
    D.pullbackIdealProduct F' =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsProductSubmodule D.inverseImageIdealSections F' := by
  rw [pullbackIdealProduct]
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.imageProductSubmodule_eq_unitImageSections
    D.inverseImageIdealUnit
    (fun Z g hg => Stacks.SheafOfModules.restrictScalars_unit_cancel_zero D.extendScalarsAdj
      D.inverseImageIdeal Z g hg)
    D.pullbackIdealToStructure F'

/-- **`(f^{-1}J)F' = I F'` for a strict morphism of thickenings.**

Both sides are the submodule of `F'` generated by the local products of a family of sections of
`O'` with the sections of `F'`: on the left the sections coming from `(f')^*J`, on the right the
sections of the defining ideal `I`. The map of ideals `(f')^*J ⟶ I` of Stacks 08M7 factors the
first family through the second, which gives `(f^{-1}J)F' ⊆ I F'` unconditionally; strictness
(Stacks 08M9) says that this map is an epimorphism, hence locally surjective on sections, and
since the membership condition of a sheaf submodule is local the reverse inclusion follows. -/
theorem pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProduct (hD : D.IsStrict)
    (F' : SheafOfModules.{w'} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O)) :
    D.pullbackIdealProduct F' = imageProductSubmodule D.idealI.incl F' := by
  have : Epi D.idealMap := hD
  rw [pullbackIdealProduct, ← D.idealMap_spec]
  exact imageProductSubmodule_comp_of_epi D.idealMap D.idealI.incl F'

end Strict

section FirstOrder

variable {X : RingedTopos.{v, u, w}} {X' : RingedTopos.{v', u', w}}
  {S : RingedTopos.{v'', u'', w''}} {S' : RingedTopos.{v''', u''', w'''}}
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})] [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w''})] [S'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w'''})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w''} RingCat.{w''})]
  [S'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w'''} RingCat.{w'''})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [S.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w''})]
  [S'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w'''})]
  [HasSheafify X'.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [X'.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  (D : MorphismOfThickenings X X' S S')

omit [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [X'.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasSheafify X'.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X'.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- The ideal product of Stacks 08MP for the square-zero ideal datum of Stacks 08MB is the
image product of its inclusion into `O'`: the two are the same infimum. -/
theorem _root_.Deformation.ToposThickening.idealProductSubmodule_eq_imageProductSubmodule
    {i : RingedToposHom X X'} (hi : FirstOrderThickening i)
    (G' : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O)) :
    idealProductSubmodule hi G' = imageProductSubmodule hi.incl G' :=
  rfl

/-- **`(f^{-1}J)F' = I F'` for a strict morphism of thickenings**, with the right-hand side the
ideal product of Stacks 08MP attached to the square-zero ideal datum of the upper thickening.

This is `Deformation.ToposThickening.MorphismOfThickenings.pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProduct`
combined with the fact that the ideal product depends on the defining ideal only through its
sections in `O'`, which for both the datum of Stacks 08MB and the datum of Stacks 08M7 are the
sections killed by `i^♯`. -/
theorem pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProductSubmodule
    (hi : FirstOrderThickening D.i) (hD : D.IsStrict)
    (F' : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O)) :
    D.pullbackIdealProduct F' = idealProductSubmodule hi F' :=
  (D.pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProduct hD F').trans
    ((IdealOfThickening.imageProductSubmodule_incl_eq D.idealI hi.idealOfThickening F').trans
      (idealProductSubmodule_eq_imageProductSubmodule hi F').symm)

/-- **`(f^{-1}J)F' = I F'` for a strict morphism of thickenings**, with both sides written as
submodules generated by explicit families of products of sections: on the left the products
`(f')^♯(j) • x` of a section `j` of `f^{-1}J` with a section `x` of `F'`, on the right the
products `α • x` of a section `α` of the square-zero ideal `I` with a section of `F'`.

This is the form in which the identity is the sentence of the source: the strictness of `(f,f')`
and `F = i^*F'` imply `F = F'/(f^{-1}J)F'`, the quotient by the right-hand side being `i_*i^*F'`
by `Deformation.ToposThickening.idealProductShortComplex_shortExact`. -/
theorem sectionsProductSubmodule_inverseImageIdealSections_eq_idealProductSubmodule
    (hi : FirstOrderThickening D.i) (hD : D.IsStrict)
    (F' : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X'.O)) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionsProductSubmodule D.inverseImageIdealSections F' =
      idealProductSubmodule hi F' :=
  (D.pullbackIdealProduct_eq_sectionsProductSubmodule F').symm.trans
    (D.pullbackIdealProduct_eq_idealProductSubmodule hi hD F')

end FirstOrder

end MorphismOfThickenings

end Deformation.ToposThickening

end
